1
00:01:49,607 --> 00:01:51,600
<i>Life is but 30,000 days.</i>

2
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,640
<i>Just 30,000 sunsets and sunrises.</i>

3
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:57,640
<i>When dreams meet the future,</i>

4
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:01,697
<i>they become
the most unforgettable moment of all.</i>

5
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:20,225
<i>For me, that moment was</i>

6
00:02:20,225 --> 00:02:24,005
<i>the surge of excitement
when I first soared into the sky.</i>

7
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:46,600
[Episode 5]
[She Soars the Skies]

8
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:54,224
Mentor, Captain Fan. We're heading back.

9
00:02:54,224 --> 00:02:55,928
- Captain, see you.
- Get some rest.

10
00:02:55,928 --> 00:02:57,952
- Okay.
- Mentor. Captain Yue.

11
00:02:57,952 --> 00:02:58,952
Thank you.

12
00:03:00,042 --> 00:03:01,408
Ruan Si Xian.

13
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,090
- You're all here.
- Mr. Fu.

14
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:11,704
- You came alone?
- I did.

15
00:03:11,704 --> 00:03:14,080
Perfect. The inaugural flight is coming up.

16
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,302
I came to check on you.

17
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,240
Let me give you an update.

18
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:22,320
The pilots have been doing well lately.

19
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:25,320
Especially Ruan.
She just finished on the simulator.

20
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,640
- She flew exceptionally well.
- Really?

21
00:03:28,519 --> 00:03:31,255
You performed well. You deserve some praise.

22
00:03:32,716 --> 00:03:34,440
You seem to be in a good mood, Mr. Fu.

23
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:35,480
I am.

24
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:38,520
[Z101 - Let's Soar Over Mountains and Seas.]
I just completed a very important task.

25
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:39,939
And I'm in great spirits.

26
00:03:42,732 --> 00:03:45,560
My task is flying planes.

27
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:50,460
Why don't you join us in the simulator
and see what it's like?

28
00:03:53,708 --> 00:03:57,280
That's an excellent suggestion.

29
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:00,520
Mr. Fu, these newly arrived simulators
are full-motion.

30
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:03,800
Once you're in,
it feels like flying a real plane.

31
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:04,960
Give it a try.

32
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:08,743
That's right. Let Ruan take you for a spin.

33
00:04:08,743 --> 00:04:10,160
She flies very steadily.

34
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:11,160
Really?

35
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:16,400
Thanks, but no. I mean, I actually tried one
before we bought them.

36
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,803
Alright.

37
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:23,484
It's already lunchtime.
Let's grab lunch together.

38
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,120
Maybe not.

39
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:30,120
Your meals might be too fancy for us.

40
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:33,800
The inaugural flight is imminent.
I'd better focus on training.

41
00:04:40,226 --> 00:04:42,240
- What about you two?
- We've already eaten.

42
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,640
I see.

43
00:04:44,531 --> 00:04:46,987
Mr. Fu, if you...

44
00:04:49,231 --> 00:04:52,725
If you need to talk to Ruan,
we can postpone the practice a bit.

45
00:04:52,725 --> 00:04:54,008
- Right, Captain Fan?
- Sure.

46
00:04:54,008 --> 00:04:57,019
It's okay. Practice is more important.

47
00:04:57,677 --> 00:04:59,710
After all, there will be plenty of chances.

48
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,499
What chances?

49
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,247
Chances, you know. You all carry on.

50
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,090
Bai Yang.

51
00:05:40,572 --> 00:05:43,949
<i>Ms. Zheng, have you decided
what we discussed earlier?</i>

52
00:05:43,949 --> 00:05:47,621
The filming and post-production
were part of the same package.

53
00:05:47,621 --> 00:05:50,504
Now you're hiring someone else
for post-production. Why?

54
00:05:50,504 --> 00:05:52,840
Ms. Zheng, I'm truly sorry.

55
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:55,191
But our contract does say exactly that.

56
00:05:55,191 --> 00:06:00,822
<i>Our company has final rights over all footage,
including final edits and usage rights.</i>

57
00:06:03,643 --> 00:06:07,200
Fine. Do whatever you want.
I've never seen a company like yours.

58
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,662
Just send the remaining payment soon.

59
00:06:16,752 --> 00:06:18,493
Hello?

60
00:06:18,493 --> 00:06:20,156
Where are you?

61
00:06:20,156 --> 00:06:25,060
This is the most undignified shoot
I've ever had.

62
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:28,960
I was treated like a tool. They use me when
they need me and toss me aside when they don't.

63
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:32,320
He was adorable as a kid.
How did he grow up to be such a jerk?

64
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:36,800
That guy is just unreliable.

65
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:40,360
Even worse, he's morally bankrupt
and utterly shameless.

66
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:44,200
Only you still have hopes for him.

67
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:47,440
You're here to work out.
Can you at least take it seriously?

68
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:50,160
Are those earphones stuck to your ears?

69
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,126
I had a meeting today.

70
00:06:52,126 --> 00:06:56,423
But you called. So I came out for you.
Now I have to take it online.

71
00:06:57,852 --> 00:07:01,040
Well... Sorry.

72
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:05,970
When something happens, you're my first call.
I forgot that you're a boss now.

73
00:07:05,970 --> 00:07:07,507
Sorry to bother you.

74
00:07:10,587 --> 00:07:15,069
Actually, you didn't bother me.

75
00:07:15,069 --> 00:07:17,587
I've been wanting to complain about
Fu Ming Yu for ages.

76
00:07:17,587 --> 00:07:19,399
But Zhu Dong always takes his side.

77
00:07:19,399 --> 00:07:23,839
Now that you're back, it's like a godsend.

78
00:07:23,839 --> 00:07:25,704
If you ever want to roast him,
I'm ready anytime.

79
00:07:25,704 --> 00:07:27,520
Anytime is good.

80
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:32,414
Now, let's go climb the wall.

81
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:37,480
You're too old for kids' games.
Why climb the wall?

82
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:39,015
Come on.

83
00:07:42,651 --> 00:07:45,421
Look at you, still scampering like a kid.

84
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:53,040
[One day to Z101's inaugural flight
at Hengshi Air]

85
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:14,231
[One day to Z101's inaugural flight
at Hengshi Air]

86
00:08:21,279 --> 00:08:24,000
Good luck on the inaugural flight.

87
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,279
- Captain Yue, how are you doing?
- Director.

88
00:08:26,279 --> 00:08:27,280
Congratulations.

89
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:29,440
- Hello, Captain Yue. Captain Fan.
- Director.

90
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:31,928
I wish you a successful inaugural flight.

91
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:34,059
Don't worry, Director.

92
00:08:34,059 --> 00:08:37,200
- Ruan.
- Mentor, I'm here.

93
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,290
- Time to go.
- Coming!

94
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:36,440
<i>Ms. Ruan.</i>

95
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:40,422
<i>I think we should go for a drink tonight.</i>

96
00:09:40,422 --> 00:09:44,600
<i>Mr. Yan, the inaugural flight is tomorrow.
I can't drink.</i>

97
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:46,840
<i>Right. No drinking then.</i>

98
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:50,000
<i>Also, don't pick me up from work next time.</i>

99
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,113
<i>I don't want people to get the wrong idea.</i>

100
00:09:56,080 --> 00:10:00,202
<i>We should book a feast tomorrow
and celebrate for Ruan.</i>

101
00:10:00,202 --> 00:10:04,003
<i>I suggest we come to my place.
It'll be more convenient.</i>

102
00:10:05,667 --> 00:10:06,998
<i>Sounds good.</i>

103
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,248
<i>You like this actor?</i>

104
00:10:12,675 --> 00:10:14,040
<i>You know him too?</i>

105
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:17,423
<i>Of course. He was super popular
when we were in high school.</i>

106
00:10:17,423 --> 00:10:19,647
<i>His drama. What was it called?</i>

107
00:10:19,647 --> 00:10:22,640
<i>- "Tennis Boy."
- Right, "Tennis Boy."</i>

108
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:25,705
<i>The girls talked about him every day.
I got sick of hearing it.</i>

109
00:10:25,705 --> 00:10:27,678
<i>Sick of it?</i>

110
00:10:28,835 --> 00:10:30,660
<i>That's because you men don't get it.</i>

111
00:10:30,660 --> 00:10:32,564
<i>You're the one who doesn't get it.</i>

112
00:10:32,564 --> 00:10:34,828
<i>Back then, the girls always said</i>

113
00:10:34,828 --> 00:10:39,332
<i>Fu Ming Yu had the same vibe
as the guy who played the lead.</i>

114
00:10:39,332 --> 00:10:40,516
<i>Who?</i>

115
00:10:40,516 --> 00:10:43,120
<i>His name was... Xiao Xun Li.</i>

116
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:46,600
<i>More like "Chestnut." Xiao Xun Li, my foot.</i>

117
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,840
<i>Besides, his name is Xiao Li Xun.</i>

118
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:51,379
<i>"Chestnut" is a fun name.</i>

119
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:58,660
How do they look alike?
Nothing alike, okay? You were all blind.

120
00:11:04,715 --> 00:11:08,459
What a coincidence. Speak of the devil.

121
00:11:15,987 --> 00:11:17,671
What did you just say?

122
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:19,634
Nothing.

123
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:29,880
<i>Do they look alike? Not really.</i>

124
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:32,657
<i>Their features are completely different.</i>

125
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:38,744
<i>But Mr. Yan meant the vibe,
not the facial features.</i>

126
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,800
<i>That's enough. He doesn't compare.</i>

127
00:11:46,242 --> 00:11:47,680
Have you been drinking?

128
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:49,564
No.

129
00:11:49,564 --> 00:11:51,626
Then why is your face so red?

130
00:11:51,626 --> 00:11:54,960
Does it have to be alcohol?

131
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,224
Maybe I'm just riding a post-clubbing high.

132
00:11:57,224 --> 00:11:59,040
You have your inaugural flight tomorrow.

133
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:01,800
Drinking before that is forbidden.

134
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:03,047
You should know that.

135
00:12:03,047 --> 00:12:05,579
I said I didn't drink.

136
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,191
Ruan Si Xian.

137
00:12:12,253 --> 00:12:16,836
- Yes, boss?
- First, Yan An is with Bo'ao Air.

138
00:12:16,836 --> 00:12:19,660
Getting close to him is inappropriate.

139
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:22,044
Mr. Fu, are you stalking me?

140
00:12:22,044 --> 00:12:25,708
Second, Yan An is a playboy.

141
00:12:25,708 --> 00:12:29,250
He changes girlfriends like clothes.
Think about it carefully.

142
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:31,120
What about you, Mr. Fu?

143
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,544
Are you a playboy too?

144
00:12:32,544 --> 00:12:34,408
Don't compare him with me.

145
00:12:44,436 --> 00:12:47,632
Spain is great in every way,
except for the food.

146
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,080
Yue Yang.

147
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:55,568
The trip to Spain
must have cost you quite a bit.

148
00:12:55,568 --> 00:12:57,240
What's wrong?

149
00:12:57,240 --> 00:13:00,151
I mean, maybe we should split the bill.

150
00:13:00,151 --> 00:13:03,094
All that matters is your happiness.

151
00:13:04,243 --> 00:13:08,600
Of course, if you want to thank me,
you can treat me to a nice dinner tonight.

152
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:10,185
- Is that all?
- Sure.

153
00:13:10,185 --> 00:13:12,000
I haven't eaten well lately, after all.

154
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,292
Let me see.

155
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:23,840
[Jiang Zi Long]

156
00:13:25,727 --> 00:13:30,071
<i>Send the money.
If you don't, I'll go to your company.</i>

157
00:13:35,961 --> 00:13:37,276
Let's go.

158
00:13:42,509 --> 00:13:45,533
Well, why don't you go home first?

159
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:46,678
Why?

160
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:50,753
I suddenly feel a bit tired.

161
00:13:50,753 --> 00:13:53,157
Weren't you fine just now?

162
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:56,264
Besides, I should be the tired one, right?

163
00:13:56,264 --> 00:13:57,920
That's not what I meant.

164
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,630
Then what did you mean?

165
00:14:01,389 --> 00:14:02,732
How about this?

166
00:14:02,732 --> 00:14:08,692
Tomorrow, I'll take you
to the best hot pot place, okay?

167
00:14:10,963 --> 00:14:13,242
Okay. Tomorrow, then.

168
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:17,584
- See you.
- Get some rest.

169
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:20,440
- I'll watch you go in.
- Let me know when you get home.

170
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,501
Okay.

171
00:14:22,457 --> 00:14:23,733
- Bye.
- Bye.

172
00:14:41,387 --> 00:14:44,693
<i>Hey, Zi Yue. You're his older sister.</i>

173
00:14:44,693 --> 00:14:47,357
<i>Help him out when he needs it.</i>

174
00:14:47,357 --> 00:14:50,861
He's your son, not mine.
Why should I support him?

175
00:14:50,861 --> 00:14:52,920
<i>You haven't sent this month's money yet.</i>

176
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:54,800
How have I not?

177
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:58,543
I send it every month.
I've just been busy this month, and I forgot.

178
00:14:58,543 --> 00:15:03,333
I have my own things to take care of.
I have things I need money for.

179
00:15:03,333 --> 00:15:06,960
<i>Zi Yue, I'm not in good health.
And your brother doesn't have a job.</i>

180
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:10,680
<i>- Look out for the family.</i>
- Then who's looking out for me?

181
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:12,845
Am I really your daughter?

182
00:15:12,845 --> 00:15:14,560
<i>Jiang Zi Yue, you ungrateful brat.</i>

183
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:17,240
<i>You make over 20,000 a month.
Who else are you going to give it to?</i>

184
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:19,800
Don't threaten me!

185
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:25,303
If you dare make a scene at my company,
and I lose my job, we'll all starve.

186
00:16:19,816 --> 00:16:23,183
[The day of
Hengshi Air Z101's inaugural flight]

187
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:45,040
<i>To Ruan's successful inaugural flight!
May you soar to success!</i>

188
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:47,960
<i>"Captain" Ruan, wish you
a safe landing on the inaugural flight!</i>

189
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:50,609
<i>Hope everything goes smoothly!</i>

190
00:17:08,396 --> 00:17:10,560
Morning, Mr. Yan.

191
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,836
You're here early. Working at Hengshi Air?

192
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:16,960
You work. I don't have to.

193
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,469
Keep up the hard work.

194
00:17:26,411 --> 00:17:27,651
Morning, Mr. Fu.

195
00:17:27,651 --> 00:17:29,516
What are you doing here so early?

196
00:17:29,516 --> 00:17:32,640
What else would I be doing?
I'm here to pick up Ms. Ruan.

197
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:36,565
I don't mean to criticize you,
but isn't Hengshi Air being a bit stingy?

198
00:17:36,565 --> 00:17:38,629
You spent so much to poach this pilot,

199
00:17:38,629 --> 00:17:40,173
yet you didn't even arrange a car for her.

200
00:17:40,173 --> 00:17:42,637
What if she couldn't get a taxi
this early in the morning?

201
00:17:42,637 --> 00:17:45,060
That's really not your concern.

202
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:46,443
Mr. Fu.

203
00:17:50,374 --> 00:17:53,840
Would it be inappropriate for me to date...

204
00:17:54,957 --> 00:17:56,775
one of your employees?

205
00:17:57,648 --> 00:18:00,760
How about this? Let's make a deal.

206
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:03,520
Your company has so many talented people.

207
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:07,240
Why don't you... let me have Ms. Ruan?

208
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:10,207
Is it even a possibility?

209
00:18:11,371 --> 00:18:13,080
More than just a possibility.

210
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:16,625
The two of us hit it off immediately.

211
00:18:16,625 --> 00:18:17,960
Is that so?

212
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:21,243
Why do I feel like she's more interested in me?

213
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:24,200
I'm more interested in you?

214
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,880
Mr. Fu, that's an interesting assumption.

215
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:30,600
No, I didn't mean it that way.

216
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:31,981
No?

217
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:37,260
- Morning, Mr. Yan.
- Morning.

218
00:18:41,221 --> 00:18:42,844
This is getting interesting.

219
00:18:42,844 --> 00:18:44,868
Leave it to me.

220
00:18:44,868 --> 00:18:46,691
What's that supposed to mean?

221
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:49,160
Be careful.

222
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,077
Fasten your seat belt.

223
00:19:09,419 --> 00:19:12,883
I don't know what kind of history
you and Fu Ming Yu have,

224
00:19:12,883 --> 00:19:16,874
but today was the first time I've seen
anyone give him the cold shoulder.

225
00:19:16,874 --> 00:19:20,098
I'm feeling absolutely fantastic right now.

226
00:19:20,098 --> 00:19:22,602
What's your history with him?

227
00:19:22,602 --> 00:19:24,146
Competitors, of course.

228
00:19:24,146 --> 00:19:27,051
The two companies split from one.

229
00:19:27,051 --> 00:19:30,274
But they still maintain
a non-zero-sum approach.

230
00:19:30,274 --> 00:19:33,720
Competing and cooperating for mutual benefit.

231
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:36,505
It's no secret that the chairmen
of Hengshi Air and Bo'ao Air

232
00:19:36,505 --> 00:19:39,800
still hang out for golf
or afternoon tea now and then.

233
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:43,020
Even Fu Ming Yu and you grew up together.

234
00:19:44,225 --> 00:19:46,025
You men and your lies.

235
00:19:46,025 --> 00:19:48,289
No wonder you're a top pilot.

236
00:19:48,289 --> 00:19:50,313
You sure know a lot.

237
00:19:50,313 --> 00:19:51,679
Unlike me.

238
00:19:51,679 --> 00:19:57,672
Growing up, my grades and behavior
were always at the bottom of the class.

239
00:19:57,672 --> 00:20:01,785
But my father kept me on a tight leash.

240
00:20:01,785 --> 00:20:05,160
I never dared to step out of line.

241
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:09,800
I always felt I was letting my teachers down
by not living up to the name of a 'dandy.'

242
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:14,824
But Fu Ming Yu always stood apart
since we were kids.

243
00:20:14,824 --> 00:20:19,249
His face is deceiving, and he's a top student.

244
00:20:19,249 --> 00:20:22,809
Teachers and classmates all liked him.
Isn't that annoying?

245
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:25,545
But here's the worst part.

246
00:20:25,545 --> 00:20:28,408
The girl I'd had a crush on for two years
but never confessed to

247
00:20:28,408 --> 00:20:31,012
suddenly came to me one day.

248
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:35,160
I thought my chance had finally come,
we even dated as friends for a month.

249
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:37,120
But in the end, she said,

250
00:20:37,120 --> 00:20:41,737
"Yan An, could you introduce me to Fu Ming Yu?"

251
00:20:42,674 --> 00:20:44,454
I was absolutely livid.

252
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:48,423
So, Ms. Ruan, thank you.

253
00:20:48,423 --> 00:20:49,728
For what?

254
00:20:49,728 --> 00:20:52,800
I have finally had my day today.

255
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,120
Thank you.

256
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:56,194
You've really made me look good.

257
00:20:59,454 --> 00:21:03,662
Whenever I see you in that uniform
and think about how you didn't join us,

258
00:21:03,662 --> 00:21:05,401
I feel deep regret.

259
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,600
But I'm a generous person.

260
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:12,366
No matter where you work,
I sincerely wish you a bright future.

261
00:21:14,897 --> 00:21:16,240
Thank you.

262
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:18,160
You can thank me later.

263
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:22,180
When we get to the airport,
I have a surprise for you.

264
00:21:23,599 --> 00:21:26,740
- What surprise?
- You'll know when we get there.

265
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:36,359
[A Transformation. A Bright New Future.]

266
00:21:36,359 --> 00:21:39,059
So, what do you think? Impressive, right?

267
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:56,120
[A Transformation. A Bright New Future.]

268
00:22:05,330 --> 00:22:07,353
[Z101 - Let's Soar Over Mountains and Seas]

269
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:29,440
Mr. Yan. Why are you here?

270
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,249
[Fu Ming Yu]

271
00:22:30,249 --> 00:22:34,305
<i>If running alone in the dark feels lonely,
then let's do it together.</i>

272
00:22:34,305 --> 00:22:36,040
Okay, see you.

273
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:37,569
Thank you.

274
00:22:40,068 --> 00:22:41,453
You're welcome.

275
00:22:41,453 --> 00:22:44,377
If you like it, I can bring you one every day.

276
00:22:47,485 --> 00:22:51,029
Do you know that
the purser used to fly international routes?

277
00:22:51,029 --> 00:22:55,453
And she was only transferred here
shortly before the Z101's inaugural flight.

278
00:22:55,453 --> 00:23:00,200
But I heard that the original roster
had Ms. Liu from our division as purser.

279
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:04,040
Given her domestic flight experience,
she is the most deserving.

280
00:23:04,040 --> 00:23:06,560
Our job looks glamorous, but in reality,

281
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:10,520
there's radiation, noise,
and the torture of jet lag.

282
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:15,064
An aircraft's inaugural flight
is a huge media moment.

283
00:23:15,064 --> 00:23:19,009
All eyes and cameras will be on you,
and you'll be in the news.

284
00:23:19,009 --> 00:23:21,192
That alone is the highlight of our career.

285
00:23:21,192 --> 00:23:23,216
How could Ms. Liu miss that?

286
00:23:23,216 --> 00:23:24,280
Isn't it a pity?

287
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,200
That's just fate.

288
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:29,080
In terms of seniority,
how is my mentor less qualified?

289
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:32,800
Ms. Liu is well-deserving,
but she happened to get sick on duty.

290
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:34,880
My mentor stepped up at the last minute.

291
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:39,065
You can feel sorry for Ms. Liu,
but don't throw shade at others.

292
00:23:39,065 --> 00:23:40,788
What are you talking about?

293
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:44,124
Nothing.

294
00:23:44,124 --> 00:23:45,749
Just some celebrity gossip.

295
00:23:45,749 --> 00:23:48,040
They never talk about anything useful.

296
00:23:48,040 --> 00:23:49,383
Alright.

297
00:23:49,383 --> 00:23:52,088
This flight mission is very special.

298
00:23:52,088 --> 00:23:55,640
The cabin isn't fully open to the public,
most passengers are invited.

299
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:59,448
Besides traditional media,
we also have social media influencers.

300
00:23:59,448 --> 00:24:04,200
Furthermore, Vice President Fu
will be on this flight.

301
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:06,103
He's heading to Lin City on business.

302
00:24:06,103 --> 00:24:08,407
So, stay sharp, everyone.

303
00:24:08,407 --> 00:24:10,834
- Am I clear?
- Yes.

304
00:24:13,868 --> 00:24:16,013
I'm Yue Yang, the captain for this flight.

305
00:24:16,013 --> 00:24:18,080
Captain Fan Lei and I
should be familiar to you all.

306
00:24:18,080 --> 00:24:20,745
As for my other two colleagues,
introduce yourselves.

307
00:24:20,745 --> 00:24:23,289
I'm the co-pilot for this flight, Lu Hua.

308
00:24:23,289 --> 00:24:26,667
Hello, everyone.
I'm the trainee pilot, Ruan Si Xian.

309
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:30,960
<i>If you hadn't quit on impulse,</i>

310
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:36,687
<i>you'd be a purser by now,
or maybe even management.</i>

311
00:24:36,687 --> 00:24:39,680
<i>Ruan, we should get together sometime.</i>

312
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,737
<i>Plenty of time for that.</i>

313
00:24:44,680 --> 00:24:48,152
<i>Do you have a waitress here named Ruan Si Xian?</i>

314
00:24:48,152 --> 00:24:49,860
<i>Yes. Why?</i>

315
00:24:54,245 --> 00:24:56,789
Is there something on my face?

316
00:24:56,789 --> 00:24:59,533
No. We just think you're pretty.

317
00:24:59,533 --> 00:25:02,557
Alright. One last thing. Some reminders.

318
00:25:02,557 --> 00:25:06,280
First, media teams will be there today.
Let's all be prepared.

319
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:09,240
Second, it might be a bit of a bumpy flight.

320
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:11,704
OMB turbulence index is five.

321
00:25:11,704 --> 00:25:14,328
Watch the seat belt sign for guidance.

322
00:25:14,328 --> 00:25:18,391
Also, in case of emergencies like a fire,
security should act first, then report.

323
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:20,208
That's all from me.

324
00:25:26,028 --> 00:25:28,982
Purser, are you okay?

325
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:32,644
I'm fine. Well, I'll just add two points.

326
00:25:32,644 --> 00:25:34,588
The hot-to-cold water ratio is 3:7.

327
00:25:34,588 --> 00:25:36,972
Mind the water temperature
so you don't burn any passengers.

328
00:25:36,972 --> 00:25:42,460
Also, make sure passengers don't switch seats.
We need to keep the load balanced.

329
00:25:42,460 --> 00:25:43,560
- Captain Yue.
- Yes?

330
00:25:43,560 --> 00:25:45,960
- Any other instructions?
- No.

331
00:25:45,960 --> 00:25:47,370
What about you guys?

332
00:25:48,604 --> 00:25:52,907
Then I wish you all the best.
Enjoy the inaugural flight.

333
00:25:52,907 --> 00:25:54,778
Good. Let's head over.

334
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,839
Ruan!

335
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:11,990
Mr. Peng, this...

336
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:15,240
Don't get me wrong. It's not from me.

337
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:19,320
Mr. Yan sent it to you.
I saw it at the door, so I brought it in.

338
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:23,800
[Captain Ruan, Smooth First Flight! Yan An.]
<i>If you like it, I can bring you one every day.</i>

339
00:26:24,610 --> 00:26:25,560
Here, take it.

340
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:28,222
Well, I thought it was a flower basket.

341
00:26:28,222 --> 00:26:30,520
- How am I supposed to hold this?
- It's awkward to hold.

342
00:26:30,520 --> 00:26:33,960
- It's too heavy.
- It is. Hold it steady. Support the bottom.

343
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:36,787
Hold it. Good. Don't move.

344
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:44,343
Ruan, don't move.

345
00:26:44,343 --> 00:26:46,768
It's heavy.

346
00:26:46,768 --> 00:26:48,752
Easy. Leave it to me.

347
00:26:48,752 --> 00:26:49,881
Let me do it.

348
00:26:49,881 --> 00:26:52,520
You can let go.

349
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:54,830
Just let go.

350
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:25,799
[A Transformation. A Bright New Future.]

351
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,480
As an aviation enthusiast,

352
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:35,279
joining the Z101's first flight
is a rare opportunity for me.

353
00:27:35,279 --> 00:27:39,680
[Successful Flight]

354
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:14,520
- Mr. Fu.
- Mr. Fu.

355
00:28:14,520 --> 00:28:16,654
Welcome aboard, Mr. Fu.

356
00:28:19,915 --> 00:28:22,223
<i>Welcome aboard, Mr. Fu.</i>

357
00:28:28,410 --> 00:28:30,223
Thank you for your hard work.

358
00:28:43,886 --> 00:28:45,359
Welcome aboard.

359
00:28:45,359 --> 00:28:47,280
- Kid, your seat is here.
- Okay, thank you.

360
00:28:47,280 --> 00:28:49,887
If you need anything, just let me know.

361
00:28:51,200 --> 00:28:52,599
Mr. Bai.

362
00:28:52,599 --> 00:28:53,880
Mr. Fu.

363
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:56,440
I have a serious question for you.

364
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:58,923
- Go ahead.
- Do you know how to make it up to a girl?

365
00:28:59,810 --> 00:29:01,713
What?

366
00:29:01,713 --> 00:29:04,200
Sir, let me show you to your seat.

367
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:06,030
Sir, your seat is here.

368
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:10,824
I said, do you know
how to make it up to a girl?

369
00:29:10,824 --> 00:29:13,827
What? Could you speak louder?

370
00:29:15,438 --> 00:29:17,279
Check your phone.

371
00:29:21,539 --> 00:29:24,364
"Do you know how to make it up to a girl?"

372
00:29:30,359 --> 00:29:32,718
Hengshi Air 5253, request line up.

373
00:29:32,718 --> 00:29:35,343
<i>Hengshi Air 5253, cleared to line up Runway 04.</i>

374
00:29:35,343 --> 00:29:38,101
Cleared to line up Runway 04, Hengshi Air 5253.

375
00:29:38,101 --> 00:29:39,626
<i>Cleared to line up Runway 04.</i>

376
00:29:39,626 --> 00:29:41,415
- Confirmed.
- Lights on.

377
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:48,665
- Line-up checklist.
- Line-up checklist.

378
00:29:48,665 --> 00:29:50,680
- Takeoff runway.
- 04.

379
00:29:50,680 --> 00:29:54,279
- 04, confirmed. TCAS.
<i>- TA only.</i>

380
00:29:54,279 --> 00:29:56,410
TA, RA. Packs 1 and 2.

381
00:29:56,410 --> 00:29:57,720
On.

382
00:29:57,720 --> 00:29:59,960
Line-up checklist complete.

383
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:03,560
- Final clear. Runway clear.
<i>- Checked.</i>

384
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:16,944
Hengshi Air 5253, ready.

385
00:30:16,944 --> 00:30:18,769
03. Wind 100 at 2 meters per second.

386
00:30:18,769 --> 00:30:20,960
Runway 04, cleared for takeoff.

387
00:30:20,960 --> 00:30:23,453
Cleared for takeoff, Runway 04.
Hengshi Air 5253.

388
00:30:23,453 --> 00:30:26,079
- Takeoff clearance confirmed.
- Confirmed.

389
00:30:28,320 --> 00:30:29,839
Stabilized.

390
00:30:29,839 --> 00:30:30,880
Takeoff.

391
00:30:30,880 --> 00:30:34,240
Manual thrust. SRS. Runway, autothrust armed.

392
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:35,240
Checked.

393
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:41,982
Thrust set.

394
00:30:41,982 --> 00:30:43,600
- 100 knots.
- Checked.

395
00:30:43,600 --> 00:30:45,138
V1, rotate.

396
00:30:49,800 --> 00:30:51,080
Positive rate.

397
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:53,161
- Gear up.
- Gear up.

398
00:30:58,000 --> 00:30:59,280
<i>Navigation.</i>

399
00:30:59,280 --> 00:31:00,440
Checked.

400
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:01,504
<i>Autopilot 1 on.</i>

401
00:31:01,504 --> 00:31:02,520
Checked.

402
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:05,543
<i>Flaps zero.</i>

403
00:31:05,543 --> 00:31:07,381
Speed checked, flaps zero.

404
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:39,425
Let me.

405
00:31:44,520 --> 00:31:45,899
Okay.

406
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:48,461
Guys, look.

407
00:31:50,040 --> 00:31:51,626
<i>Cover for me. I need to use the lavatory.</i>

408
00:31:51,626 --> 00:31:52,767
Okay, I got it.

409
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:07,196
- Mr. Fu.
- Mr. Fu.

410
00:32:30,989 --> 00:32:32,371
What now?

411
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:35,983
Come out first.

412
00:32:35,983 --> 00:32:40,469
Mr. Fu, why the rush? You really can't hold it?

413
00:32:44,400 --> 00:32:46,066
Watch out! Be careful.

414
00:32:53,123 --> 00:32:55,650
Go on. I'm heading back.

415
00:32:58,440 --> 00:33:00,438
Actually, what I want to say is...

416
00:33:03,638 --> 00:33:04,809
I'm sorry.

417
00:33:13,233 --> 00:33:16,809
Mr. Fu, I still suggest you
use the lavatory now.

418
00:33:16,809 --> 00:33:19,360
There will be turbulence soon.

419
00:33:19,360 --> 00:33:21,265
The lavatory might be closed.

420
00:33:21,265 --> 00:33:23,455
Also, stay safe.

421
00:33:35,796 --> 00:33:37,533
She's impossible to appease.

422
00:33:41,074 --> 00:33:42,339
Mr. Fu.

423
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:07,985
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

424
00:34:10,635 --> 00:34:12,259
Let me say a few words first.

425
00:34:12,259 --> 00:34:14,082
- That's satisfying.
- Go on.

426
00:34:14,082 --> 00:34:17,680
When Ruan left Hengshi Air,
a bunch of people were gossiping.

427
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:19,825
I was so angry that I wanted to fight them.

428
00:34:19,825 --> 00:34:21,256
Well, look at it now.

429
00:34:21,256 --> 00:34:24,560
"Captain" Ruan's photo is all over Hengshi Air.

430
00:34:24,560 --> 00:34:28,225
Now that's a triumphant return.
Couldn't be more satisfying.

431
00:34:28,225 --> 00:34:29,560
Speech over.

432
00:34:29,560 --> 00:34:32,737
Alright, eat. The meat is getting overcooked.

433
00:34:36,480 --> 00:34:39,120
Today is our superstar's inaugural flight.

434
00:34:39,120 --> 00:34:40,560
Why are you so calm?

435
00:34:40,560 --> 00:34:43,785
Yeah. Three generations of female pilots
in one frame.

436
00:34:43,785 --> 00:34:46,128
The news is trending.

437
00:34:46,128 --> 00:34:50,040
And the whole airport
is filled with Ruan's photos.

438
00:34:50,040 --> 00:34:51,840
Aren't you happy?

439
00:34:55,292 --> 00:34:58,690
Or did something unpleasant happen today?

440
00:35:00,746 --> 00:35:02,720
Nothing unpleasant.

441
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:05,705
I feel like my wish has finally come true.

442
00:35:05,705 --> 00:35:07,760
Is that the face of someone
whose wish came true?

443
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:09,762
Why don't you look in the mirror?

444
00:35:10,795 --> 00:35:14,659
Actually, I've imagined this countless times.

445
00:35:14,659 --> 00:35:18,522
I thought today would be the most memorable

446
00:35:18,522 --> 00:35:21,371
and most exciting day of my life.

447
00:35:21,371 --> 00:35:25,515
But when I sat in the jump seat
as a trainee pilot,

448
00:35:25,515 --> 00:35:28,777
I realized that I wanted even more.

449
00:35:28,777 --> 00:35:33,480
I kept thinking about
when I'd become a real co-pilot,

450
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:35,265
then a real captain.

451
00:35:35,265 --> 00:35:38,221
I kept dreaming bigger.

452
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:42,423
Am I being too greedy?

453
00:35:42,423 --> 00:35:44,487
How is that greedy?

454
00:35:44,487 --> 00:35:46,720
Dreams are meant to be big.

455
00:35:46,720 --> 00:35:48,920
Who says women can't be ambitious?

456
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:53,033
Ambition drives you to live life
to the fullest with passion.

457
00:35:53,033 --> 00:35:55,259
Exactly. Xuan is right.

458
00:36:00,195 --> 00:36:01,405
A toast to you two.

459
00:36:01,405 --> 00:36:04,765
The two biggest backers
in making my dream come true.

460
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:11,013
If it weren't for Xuan's generous support,

461
00:36:11,013 --> 00:36:15,184
my dream would've died
before I even got into the academy.

462
00:36:16,613 --> 00:36:18,916
And our head of logistics, Xiao Zhen.

463
00:36:18,916 --> 00:36:24,362
Without your constant feeding,
I might have never made it this far.

464
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:30,409
I don't have much family in this world.

465
00:36:30,409 --> 00:36:36,346
You are my last link to this world.

466
00:36:39,819 --> 00:36:42,363
Hey, why are you being so formal?

467
00:36:42,363 --> 00:36:45,331
Look at her, isn't she annoying?

468
00:36:45,331 --> 00:36:46,875
She really is.

469
00:36:46,875 --> 00:36:48,600
Getting all sentimental.

470
00:36:48,600 --> 00:36:51,395
I'm going to cry. My makeup will be ruined.

471
00:36:51,395 --> 00:36:53,219
You'll have to pay for it.

472
00:36:53,219 --> 00:36:55,334
Alright, come on. A toast to you two.

473
00:36:55,334 --> 00:36:56,679
Don't mention it.

474
00:36:56,679 --> 00:36:58,045
No problem.

475
00:36:58,045 --> 00:36:59,320
- To you both.
- No problem.

476
00:36:59,320 --> 00:37:00,760
No problem.

477
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:02,400
Don't mention it.

478
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:06,293
- You're both big bosses. I'm not worthy.
- Alright. Everyone up.

479
00:37:07,240 --> 00:37:09,635
Let me say a few words.

480
00:37:09,635 --> 00:37:15,318
Today means a lot to all of us.

481
00:37:15,318 --> 00:37:18,357
The past is the path we've walked.

482
00:37:18,357 --> 00:37:21,223
We won't forget it,
but we won't dwell on it either.

483
00:37:22,040 --> 00:37:24,785
This toast is to the future.

484
00:37:24,785 --> 00:37:30,381
May we have a bright future
and fulfill our dreams.

485
00:37:30,381 --> 00:37:33,499
- To a bright future and our dreams.
- To a bright future and our dreams!

486
00:37:33,499 --> 00:37:35,784
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

487
00:38:14,636 --> 00:38:17,660
It's the new female pilot, Ruan Si Xian.

488
00:38:17,660 --> 00:38:19,000
Really?

489
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:21,431
Her resume is way too impressive.

490
00:38:21,431 --> 00:38:23,920
She's always been impressive.

491
00:38:23,920 --> 00:38:26,904
Back when she was a flight attendant,
she was outstanding too.

492
00:38:26,904 --> 00:38:30,320
If she hadn't left,
she'd likely be a purser by now.

493
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:33,144
But I don't get it.
Why did she come back to Hengshi Air?

494
00:38:33,144 --> 00:38:35,968
I heard many airlines were fighting over her.

495
00:38:35,968 --> 00:38:40,240
Yeah, why? And I've heard about her history.

496
00:38:40,240 --> 00:38:42,000
Doesn't she feel embarrassed?

497
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:46,259
Could it be she still has feelings for Mr. Fu?

498
00:38:46,259 --> 00:38:49,883
If that's the case, everything makes sense.

499
00:38:49,883 --> 00:38:51,426
What makes sense?

500
00:38:51,426 --> 00:38:53,520
When we're talking about outstanding women,

501
00:38:53,520 --> 00:38:56,104
can we not bring up baseless gossip?

502
00:38:56,104 --> 00:38:59,080
I think there's no smoke without fire.

503
00:38:59,080 --> 00:39:03,243
Since it's being spread with so many details,
it's probably true.

504
00:39:03,243 --> 00:39:07,787
How can you be sure those rumor mongers
don't have ulterior motives?

505
00:39:07,787 --> 00:39:10,891
Nothing stays hidden if you never do wrong.

506
00:39:10,891 --> 00:39:11,978
Exactly.

507
00:39:11,978 --> 00:39:15,694
If you're so curious, why don't you ask me?

508
00:39:15,694 --> 00:39:17,640
I'm easy to talk to.

509
00:39:17,640 --> 00:39:20,810
Come ask, and I'll tell you everything.

510
00:39:22,640 --> 00:39:24,863
As for why I returned to Hengshi Air,

511
00:39:24,863 --> 00:39:28,047
Mr. Fu's office is always open to you.

512
00:39:28,047 --> 00:39:29,893
Go and ask him yourself.

513
00:39:54,659 --> 00:39:55,883
What time is it?

514
00:39:55,883 --> 00:39:57,062
It's 9:15.

515
00:39:58,880 --> 00:40:00,609
Let's go back to Mingchen.

516
00:40:01,930 --> 00:40:05,275
Well, during the meeting this morning,
your phone was off.

517
00:40:05,275 --> 00:40:07,498
Your mother called.

518
00:40:07,498 --> 00:40:09,482
She said you haven't been home in a while.

519
00:40:09,482 --> 00:40:11,800
It's too late today. Maybe tomorrow.

520
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:12,851
Okay.

521
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:28,414
Pull over.

522
00:40:33,669 --> 00:40:36,400
Bai Yang, take my luggage up.

523
00:40:36,400 --> 00:40:37,400
Sure thing.

524
00:41:05,707 --> 00:41:07,357
You just got off the plane?

525
00:41:10,101 --> 00:41:11,667
<i>Is it even a possibility?</i>

526
00:41:11,667 --> 00:41:13,347
<i>More than just a possibility.</i>

527
00:41:13,347 --> 00:41:14,772
<i>Is that so?</i>

528
00:41:14,772 --> 00:41:18,080
<i>Why do I feel like she's more interested in me?</i>

529
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:22,305
<i>Could it be she still has feelings for Mr. Fu?</i>

530
00:41:22,305 --> 00:41:26,574
<i>If that's the case, everything makes sense.</i>

531
00:41:28,955 --> 00:41:33,499
Today I finally learned what they mean by
"Fish rot from the head down."

532
00:41:33,499 --> 00:41:34,820
What do you mean?

533
00:41:40,040 --> 00:41:42,501
- Let me help you.
- I have hands.

534
00:41:55,933 --> 00:41:57,418
Ruan Si...

535
00:42:06,040 --> 00:42:08,630
I'm telling you, if you touch me again,

536
00:42:08,630 --> 00:42:12,214
I'll sue you for sexual harassment,
even if you are my boss.

537
00:42:12,214 --> 00:42:13,634
Touch you?

538
00:42:14,611 --> 00:42:16,284
- Sexual harassment?
- Yes.

539
00:42:27,576 --> 00:42:29,000
Ruan Si Xian.

540
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:32,825
What do I have to do to make it up to you?

541
00:42:32,825 --> 00:42:34,244
Are you finished?

542
00:42:34,917 --> 00:42:37,678
Then write it on your forehead.

543
00:42:55,645 --> 00:42:57,566
- Let's go back to Huguang.
- What?

544
00:43:00,372 --> 00:43:01,577
Go home.

545
00:43:17,280 --> 00:43:18,354
Let's go.

